# Everything here can change what gets checked, who is a member, or what runs on
# a member's machine. Two administrators must approve any change.
#
# NOTE the form of the name: a team is written @organisation/team. Written as a
# bare @polymath-admins it matches nobody, silently, and the file would look
# correct while enforcing nothing. The team must exist in the polymath-scl
# organisation before these lines do anything.
/.github/      @polymath-scl/polymath-admins
/polymath      @polymath-scl/polymath-admins
/tests/        @polymath-scl/polymath-admins
/people/       @polymath-scl/polymath-admins
/LICENSES/     @polymath-scl/polymath-admins
# Onboarding tells new members how to protect their keys and their accounts. Wrong
# advice here is a security problem, not a documentation problem.
/onboarding/   @polymath-scl/polymath-admins
